1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:07,666
Agent Garrett helps you watch your website, follow identity exposure leads, and understand what needs

2
00:00:07,666 --> 00:00:14,050
attention. This walkthrough uses the real interface. The demonstration account and example incidents

3
00:00:14,050 --> 00:00:15,032
are simulated.

4
00:00:16,332 --> 00:00:24,307
Open agent dot garrett stimpson dot ca and choose Sign in. Cloudflare handles your account. New users

5
00:00:24,307 --> 00:00:28,999
create a Cloudflare account; returning users use their existing login.

6
00:00:30,299 --> 00:00:37,432
Finish Cloudflare’s verification and review the requested permissions. We skip private account entry

7
00:00:37,432 --> 00:00:44,016
in this recording. Your workspace brings together protection, conversations, activity, and settings.

8
00:00:45,316 --> 00:00:51,739
Choose Get started, then Protect my website. The guide walks through your goal, your plan, your

9
00:00:51,739 --> 00:00:56,958
agent, and what you want to protect. No terminal or code is needed.

10
00:00:58,258 --> 00:01:05,073
For automatic protection, choose the paid Agent plan at four dollars and ninety-nine cents Canadian

11
00:01:05,073 --> 00:01:11,433
per month. The card-required three-day trial covers the MCP and backend API tools; automatic

12
00:01:11,433 --> 00:01:13,705
protection starts with paid access.

13
00:01:15,005 --> 00:01:21,994
The live app opens secure Stripe Checkout. Review the price and enter your own payment details there.

14
00:01:21,994 --> 00:01:26,517
This recording skips payment and continues with a sample paid plan.

15
00:01:27,817 --> 00:01:34,285
Choose the Cloudflare account you want Garrett to connect to. If setup is incomplete, open

16
00:01:34,285 --> 00:01:41,614
Cloudflare, finish its free Workers setup, and check again. You do not need to transfer a domain.

17
00:01:42,914 --> 00:01:50,299
Give the agent a name you will recognize, such as My security operator. Check Cloudflare setup.

18
00:01:50,299 --> 00:01:55,837
Garrett hosts the agent backend; your account receives a small connection Worker.

19
00:01:57,137 --> 00:02:04,345
Select Deploy instance. On a new real workspace, the first build can take several minutes. Wait for

20
00:02:04,345 --> 00:02:09,009
the ready state, or use Check agent readiness to try again.

21
00:02:10,309 --> 00:02:17,868
Continue to Put Garrett to work. Enter a website you own or manage. Your public website address tells

22
00:02:17,868 --> 00:02:19,967
Garrett exactly what to watch.

23
00:02:21,267 --> 00:02:27,251
Watch checks public availability and selected changes. Investigate adds bounded evidence gathering.

24
00:02:27,251 --> 00:02:34,731
Here we choose Investigate, a five-minute schedule, and text that should appear. Confirm you are

25
00:02:34,731 --> 00:02:37,224
authorized to monitor the site.

26
00:02:38,524 --> 00:02:45,746
Select Start protecting my website. Garrett schedules cloud checks. The saved baseline here is sample

27
00:02:45,746 --> 00:02:50,562
data; your account shows the observations from its own checks.

28
00:02:51,862 --> 00:02:59,120
Open Websites to review the mode, last check, next wake, and recorded activity. A successful check is

29
00:02:59,120 --> 00:03:04,244
a last-known observation. Look at the timestamp when deciding what it means.

30
00:03:05,544 --> 00:03:12,297
For a supported Cloudflare website Worker, open Protection settings and choose Handle. This adds a

31
00:03:12,297 --> 00:03:18,600
specific recovery action: restoring a healthy version you approve after a newer deployment repeatedly

32
00:03:18,600 --> 00:03:19,951
returns server errors.

33
00:03:21,251 --> 00:03:27,800
Load eligible website Workers and select the one serving your site. Read the approval carefully.

34
00:03:27,800 --> 00:03:32,603
Garrett verifies the healthy version before saving permission to restore it.

35
00:03:33,903 --> 00:03:40,643
Save the mode and check that the approved healthy version is listed. Handle does not edit your site

36
00:03:40,643 --> 00:03:45,510
or remove intruders. It recovers the approved Worker version and checks the result.

37
00:03:46,810 --> 00:03:53,620
Open Email alerts. Enter an address you control and turn on service alerts. This is how Garrett can

38
00:03:53,620 --> 00:03:58,537
tell you when a website needs attention or an investigation has an update.

39
00:03:59,837 --> 00:04:06,999
Save your email preferences, then open the confirmation link sent to your inbox. Alerts stay off

40
00:04:06,999 --> 00:04:11,475
until you confirm. We skip inbox access in this recording.

41
00:04:12,775 --> 00:04:19,791
After confirmation, check that Email alerts are on and send a test. Accepted means the sending

42
00:04:19,791 --> 00:04:25,492
service accepted the email. Check your inbox and spam folder to confirm delivery.

43
00:04:26,792 --> 00:04:34,083
Open Identity protection and add a monitoring target. You can watch an email address, full name,

44
00:04:34,083 --> 00:04:41,374
username, company, or domain. Add only your own identity or one you are authorized to represent.

45
00:04:42,674 --> 00:04:48,702
Enter the address and read the ownership consent. Public leak-post search has a separate opt-in

46
00:04:48,702 --> 00:04:55,131
because it sends the target to that search provider. Here, we leave that optional search off.

47
00:04:56,431 --> 00:05:02,609
Choose Verify and protect this address, then confirm address ownership through the email link. A

48
00:05:02,609 --> 00:05:09,199
saved target is not the same as a completed source check. Check its status and coverage.

49
00:05:10,499 --> 00:05:16,164
After verification, new leads appear under Findings, attribution and activity. This sample notice

50
00:05:16,164 --> 00:05:23,571
demonstrates the review screen. An exact mention is a lead to investigate; it does not establish a

51
00:05:23,571 --> 00:05:25,750
breach or who caused it.

52
00:05:27,050 --> 00:05:33,262
Review the containment checklist and removal-request draft. Use official service channels to change

53
00:05:33,262 --> 00:05:39,474
passwords, revoke sessions, or request removal. Record actions you actually completed. Garrett can

54
00:05:39,474 --> 00:05:45,686
recheck sources, but a missing mention does not prove every copy was erased.

55
00:05:46,986 --> 00:05:53,986
Open Agent tasks and create a runtime task. Tater-tot is Garrett’s persistent work cycle: recall

56
00:05:53,986 --> 00:06:00,987
useful context, choose an allowed action, inspect the result, measure progress, and remember what it

57
00:06:00,987 --> 00:06:01,453
learned.

58
00:06:02,753 --> 00:06:10,244
Ask for a report supported by evidence. For example: review my saved website findings and assets,

59
00:06:10,244 --> 00:06:16,330
explain what needs attention, and separate confirmed observations from unanswered questions. The task

60
00:06:16,330 --> 00:06:20,075
tools define which saved evidence it may read.

61
00:06:21,375 --> 00:06:27,929
Save the task. Automatic work normally advances one step per five-minute heartbeat. You can leave

62
00:06:27,929 --> 00:06:35,357
this page. For the next example, we advance the sample task so you can see each stage.

63
00:06:36,657 --> 00:06:44,197
Open the task context. The sample cycle chooses a findings tool, records the intent before execution,

64
00:06:44,197 --> 00:06:50,794
and saves the returned evidence. A separate measurement step assesses what that evidence supports.

65
00:06:52,094 --> 00:06:59,092
Expand Observed tool evidence. This is where you check the actual result behind a summary. A tool

66
00:06:59,092 --> 00:07:04,032
error, missing source, or old observation should remain visible as a gap.

67
00:07:05,332 --> 00:07:12,158
Open Extended memory. Owner notes and useful observations stay with this agent context. The next

68
00:07:12,158 --> 00:07:16,254
iteration can recall them instead of beginning from scratch.

69
00:07:17,554 --> 00:07:23,827
Save a short memory note about your priorities, expected evidence, and existing approval boundaries.

70
00:07:23,827 --> 00:07:28,757
Notes guide the work; they do not expand the agent’s permissions.

71
00:07:30,057 --> 00:07:37,597
You remain in control. Pause task stops its scheduled progress. Pausing this task does not pause

72
00:07:37,597 --> 00:07:42,309
separate website or identity monitors; those have their own controls.

73
00:07:43,609 --> 00:07:50,836
The saved priorities are still here after the pause. Memory is useful context, not independent proof.

74
00:07:50,836 --> 00:07:56,256
Check the source and timestamp before treating a saved observation as current.

75
00:07:57,556 --> 00:08:04,982
Resume the task when you are ready. In this sample, a second evidence step leads to owner review.

76
00:08:04,982 --> 00:08:11,996
Tasks also stop at their limits or after repeated lack of progress. More activity alone is not

77
00:08:11,996 --> 00:08:12,408
success.

78
00:08:13,708 --> 00:08:20,364
Here is a shortened, scripted incident replay. A newer deployment repeatedly returns server errors.

79
00:08:20,364 --> 00:08:27,494
The healthy version was already approved, so the sample recovery restores that version and schedules

80
00:08:27,494 --> 00:08:28,445
follow-up checks.

81
00:08:29,745 --> 00:08:36,449
Open Evidence and activity, then Agent memory and evidence. Review the observations, chosen actions,

82
00:08:36,449 --> 00:08:43,152
recovery receipt, and remaining uncertainty. This is how you inspect what the operator did.

83
00:08:44,452 --> 00:08:51,077
The sample follow-up probes returned HTTP two hundred and the expected text. That supports recovered

84
00:08:51,077 --> 00:08:58,144
availability at that time. It does not establish attribution or prove that an intruder was removed.

85
00:08:59,444 --> 00:09:05,797
Live activity brings tool starts, returned results, measurements, and updates together. Filters help

86
00:09:05,797 --> 00:09:14,106
you focus. Reading these saved logs does not itself wake the agent container or invoke the model.

87
00:09:15,406 --> 00:09:22,264
Open Chat and choose the website, task, or general workspace you want to discuss. Shared contexts

88
00:09:22,264 --> 00:09:25,693
keep the conversation attached to the relevant evidence.

89
00:09:26,993 --> 00:09:33,078
A useful question is: explain the latest evidence, what you checked, what changed, and what still

90
00:09:33,078 --> 00:09:38,021
needs my attention. You do not need to know tool names to ask.

91
00:09:39,321 --> 00:09:45,811
The sample answer explains the recorded retest and the next useful owner actions. It distinguishes

92
00:09:45,811 --> 00:09:51,868
saved evidence from a new live check. Ask for observation times and unresolved gaps.

93
00:09:53,168 --> 00:10:00,223
Workspace details explains the workflow and offers task controls. Chat uses read-only evidence tools.

94
00:10:00,223 --> 00:10:07,279
Starting a task or changing protection settings is a deliberate action; conversation does not

95
00:10:07,279 --> 00:10:09,294
silently broaden recovery approval.

96
00:10:10,594 --> 00:10:17,701
You can also connect NL-Veil or another MCP client with an instance URL and key. The documentation

97
00:10:17,701 --> 00:10:23,971
describes the one hundred and sixty-six tool catalog. Dashboard protection works without an API key

98
00:10:23,971 --> 00:10:26,061
or an open AI app.

99
00:10:27,361 --> 00:10:34,502
Before leaving, confirm the correct website and mode, a recent check, the next scheduled wake,

100
00:10:34,502 --> 00:10:41,167
verified email alerts, and the identity targets you intended to watch. Review any source-coverage

101
00:10:41,167 --> 00:10:41,643
gaps.

102
00:10:42,943 --> 00:10:50,738
Pause a website here when you want its checks to stop. The card shows that the next wake is paused.

103
00:10:50,738 --> 00:10:54,635
Use the corresponding controls for identity monitors and agent tasks.

104
00:10:55,935 --> 00:11:03,028
Resume and confirm the next wake. Your computer can be off while enabled cloud checks continue within

105
00:11:03,028 --> 00:11:09,287
your plan and allowances. Garrett protects configured websites and digital identities; it is not a

106
00:11:09,287 --> 00:11:13,042
device-wide firewall or a guarantee of complete internet coverage.
